---Metadata property bag.
---@class azure.securityinsights.MetadataProperties
---@field contentId? string Static ID for the content. Used to identify dependencies and content from solutions or community. Hard-coded/static for out of the box content and solutions. Can be optionally set for user created content to define dependencies. If an active content item is made from a template, both will have the same contentId.
---@field parentId string Full parent resource ID of the content item the metadata is for. This is the full resource ID including the scope (subscription and resource group)
---@field version? string Version of the content. Default and recommended format is numeric (e.g. 1, 1.0, 1.0.0, 1.0.0.0), following ARM template best practices. Can also be any string, but then we cannot guarantee any version checks
---@field kind string The kind of content the metadata is for.
---@field source? azure.securityinsights.MetadataSource Source of the content. This is where/how it was created.
---@field author? azure.securityinsights.MetadataAuthor The creator of the content item.
---@field support? azure.securityinsights.MetadataSupport Support information for the metadata - type, name, contact information
---@field dependencies? azure.securityinsights.MetadataDependencies Dependencies for the content item, what other content items it requires to work. Can describe more complex dependencies using a recursive/nested structure. For a single dependency an id/kind/version can be supplied or operator/criteria for complex formats.
---@field categories? azure.securityinsights.MetadataCategories Categories for the solution content item
---@field providers? azure.securityinsights.MetadataPropertiesProvidersList Providers for the solution content item
---@field firstPublishDate? string first publish date of solution content item
---@field lastPublishDate? string last publish date of solution content item
---@field customVersion? string The custom version of the content. A optional free text
---@field contentSchemaVersion? string Schema version of the content. Can be used to distinguish between different flow based on the schema version
---@field icon? string the icon identifier. this id can later be fetched from the solution template
---@field threatAnalysisTactics? azure.securityinsights.MetadataPropertiesThreatAnalysisTacticsList the tactics the resource covers
---@field threatAnalysisTechniques? azure.securityinsights.MetadataPropertiesThreatAnalysisTechniquesList the techniques the resource covers, these have to be aligned with the tactics being used
---@field previewImages? azure.securityinsights.MetadataPropertiesPreviewImagesList preview image file names. These will be taken from the solution artifacts
---@field previewImagesDark? azure.securityinsights.MetadataPropertiesPreviewImagesDarkList preview image file names. These will be taken from the solution artifacts. used for dark theme support

